Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
"1","GPIO","Independent control register for each GPIO","gpio_reg_wr_rd_test","Validate GPIO register default values and read/write behavior for GPIO 8 through GPIO 27 control/data registers. For each register, verify the reset default (with bit0 masked), then perform masked write operations using multiple data patterns and confirm readback equals the expected value considering readable and writable bit masks. Registers marked non-readable or non-writable are skipped.","test_case() performs two validations: (1) chk_rst_val(): Iterates over addr_array[0..CNT-1]; for each address, if skip_rst_array[i]==1 → continue. If read_mask_array[i]==0 → continue (not readable). Reads data_rd = read_reg(addr); computes data = (data_rd & 0xfffffffe); compares against default_value_array[i]. On mismatch increments def_fail_cnt and logs failure; otherwise logs pass under DEBUG_DISPLAY. (2) chk_rd_wr(): For each pattern in chk_val[6]={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0xf5f5f5f5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}, sets data_wr and writes to each address if skip_array[i]==1 → continue, and if write_mask_array[i]!=0 then write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])). Then reads back for each address if not skipped and if both write_mask_array[i]!=0 and read_mask_array[i]!=0: data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); computes wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff); expected exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])). Compares data_rd vs exp_val; on mismatch increments wr_fail_cnt and logs failure; otherwise logs pass under DEBUG_DISPLAY. At end, if def_fail_cnt>0 or wr_fail_cnt>0 then finish(1) else finish(0). soft_reset_chk() is disabled by #ifdef 0 and not executed.","NA","NA","NA","NA","During default checks the least significant bit is masked off to avoid false mismatches due to input behavior; ensure external GPIO inputs are stable and not driven to force unintended levels. Registers that are non-readable or non-writable per mask are intentionally skipped. Expected readback preserves default values on non-writable bits while verifying written bits according to the writable and readable masks.","1. Read and record the default reset value of each GPIO register (gp0_gpio_8 through gpio_27) that is marked as readable; ignore bit0 and compare against the predefined default values for each register.
2. For each of the data patterns {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}, write the pattern masked by the register’s writable mask to each GPIO register that is marked as writable.
3. Read back each written register using the readable mask and verify the value equals the expected composition of written bits (writable and readable) and preserved default bits (non-writable but readable).
4. Skip any register instance flagged as non-readable or non-writable as per masks and record such skips.
5. Declare the test PASS only if no default mismatches and no write/readback mismatches are detected across all registers and patterns; otherwise declare FAIL.","- Initialize def_fail_cnt=0, wr_fail_cnt=0.
- chk_rst_val():
  - For i=0..CNT-1: addr=addr_array[i]. If skip_rst_array[i]==1 → continue. If read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 → continue.
  - data_rd=read_reg(addr); data=(data_rd & 0xFFFFFFFE).
  - If data == default_value_array[i] → (optional DEBUG log PASS); else def_fail_cnt++ and log failure with addr, expected, read_data.
- chk_rd_wr():
  - chk_val[6]={0xFFFFFFFF,0xAAAAAAAA,0x55555555,0xF5F5F5F5,0xA5A5A5A5,0xFFFF0000}.
  - For each pattern j: data_wr=chk_val[j].
    - Write phase: For i=0..CNT-1: addr=addr_array[i]. If skip_array[i]==1 → continue. If write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 → continue. Else write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])).
    - Read/verify phase: For i=0..CNT-1: addr=addr_array[i]. If skip_array[i]==1 → continue. If write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 → continue. If read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 → continue. Else:
      - data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]).
      - wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xFFFFFFFF).
      - exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])).
      - If data_rd == exp_val → (optional DEBUG log PASS); else wr_fail_cnt++ and log failure with addr, expected, read.
- If (def_fail_cnt>0 || wr_fail_cnt>0) finish(1) else finish(0).
- soft_reset_chk() is not executed (#ifdef 0).","gp0_gpio_8, gpio_9, gpio_10, gpio_11, gpio_12, gpio_13, gpio_14, gpio_15, gpio_16, gpio_17, gpio_18, gpio_19, gpio_20, gpio_21, gpio_22, gpio_23, gpio_24, gpio_25, gpio_26, gpio_27","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27","- Default value verification: For each readable GPIO register (gp0_gpio_8..gpio_27), the read value with bit0 masked (AND 0xFFFFFFFE) must equal its predefined default value.
- Write/readback verification: For each data pattern and for each register that is both writable and readable, the readback value (after applying the readable mask) must equal the expected combination of written bits (within the writable+readable mask) and preserved default bits (for non-writable but readable positions).
- Overall result: PASS if no mismatches are reported across all checks; otherwise FAIL.","- Default check pass condition: (read_reg(addr) & 0xFFFFFFFE) == default_value_array[i]. If false → def_fail_cnt++.
- Write/read check pass condition per address and pattern: data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); wr_n=(write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xFFFFFFFF); exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); PASS if (data_rd == exp_val), else wr_fail_cnt++.
- Test conclusion: finish(0) if (def_fail_cnt==0 && wr_fail_cnt==0); else finish(1).","Not","#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include "test_common.h"
#include "test_define.c"
#include <gpio/gpio_def.h>
#include <gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000
#define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000
#define CNT 49","const unsigned long int addr_array[20]={MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27,};

const unsigned int default_value_array[20]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_DEFAULT_VAL,};

const unsigned int read_mask_array[20]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_READ_MASK,};

const unsigned int write_mask_array[20]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_WRITE_MASK,};"},
{"path":"Test_Output/GPIO/TestPlan/GPIO_TestPlan.xlsx","content":"Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
\"2\",\"GPIO\",\"interrupts can be generated based on positive edge or negative edge or level high or level low detection at GPIO input\",\"test_gpio_negedge_intr_en\",\"Verify that a negative-edge transition on GPIO pads 8–39 generates an interrupt per pin. Route the GPIO interrupt to the system, configure each pad for negedge detection, enable per-pin and group interrupt, toggle the external pin from high to low to create a falling edge, and confirm the ISR runs, sets/clears group status, and clears per-pin raw status without timeout.\",\"test_case(): Initializes test_err=0. Conditionally enables GIC IRQ (87 for GPIO0, 88 for GPIO1). Enables system-level interrupt routing via MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 with the instance-specific bit (LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR or LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR). Initializes the external GPIO drive register at 0xA0243ffc to 0xFFFFFFFF. For i=0..31: addr1=MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4); writes (1<<20)|(1<<18)|(1<<16) to configure per-pin settings (includes raw-clear and negedge enable), waits 10 cycles. For each i: wr_val=1<<i; clears per-pin raw via MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1=wr_val; enables per-pin interrupt via MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1=wr_val; waits 10; sets int_pend=1; drives 0xA0243ffc to 0xFFFFFFFF, waits 30; drives 0xA0243ffc to ~wr_val to generate a falling edge only on the selected pin; then polls with timeout (5000 iterations with wait_on(10)) until ISR clears int_pend. On timeout, logs error and increments test_err. At end, finish(test_err).
Default_IRQHandler(): Computes local_wr=1<<i; sets int_pend=0; writes 0xA0243ffc to 0xFFFFFFFF; reads per-pin register raddr=MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) into rdata; if (rdata & 0x1)!=0, increments test_err (unexpected input level). If ((rdata & 0x2)!=0x0), reads group status rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if ((rdata_grp & local_wr)==0) increments test_err (missing bit). Then reprograms per-pin register (1<<20)|(1<<16) to clear raw; writes MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1=local_wr; re-reads group status and expects 0. Clears system raw status via MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 using instance bit and calls GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88) based on instance.\",\"NA\",\"ISR\",\"NA\",\"NA\",\"External drive register 0xA0243ffc is used to create controlled negedge transitions; ensure only the targeted GPIO toggles to avoid false interrupts. The ISR must clear both per-pin raw status and group status before re-enabling. Timeouts indicate missing interrupt signaling or routing.\",\"1. Enable the appropriate GIC interrupt line for the target GPIO instance and route the GPIO interrupt in the system register (INTR_EN1 with the GPIO instance bit).\n2. Configure each GPIO pad control register (gp0_gpio_8 through gpio_39 range via base + index) to enable negative-edge detection and clear any latched raw status.\n3. For each pin (8–39), clear its raw status, enable the per-pin interrupt in INTR1_INTR_EN1, and generate a falling edge on that pin; wait for the ISR to service within the timeout.\n4. In the ISR, verify the group interrupt status (INTR1_INTR_STS1) reflects the expected pin bit, clear the per-pin raw status, confirm group status clears to 0, and clear the corresponding system raw status (RAW_STCR1).\n5. Report PASS only if every pin generates and services a negedge interrupt without timeout and all status registers are correctly set and cleared; otherwise FAIL.\",\"- test_err=0; optionally GIC_EnableIRQ(87/88).\n- write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIOx_INTR) for selected instance.\n- write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF).\n- For i in [0..31]: addr1=MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4); write (1<<20)|(1<<18)|(1<<16); wait_on(10).\n- For i in [0..31]: wr_val=1<<i; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, wr_val); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); int_pend=1; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); wait_on(30); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, ~wr_val); poll while(int_pend && timeout--) wait_on(10); on timeout log error and test_err++.\n- finish(test_err).\n- Default_IRQHandler(): local_wr=1<<i; int_pend=0; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); raddr=base+(i*4); rdata=read_reg(raddr); if (rdata & 0x1)!=0 then test_err++;\n  if (rdata & 0x2)!=0: rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if ((rdata_grp & local_wr)==0) test_err++;\n  write_reg(base+(i*4), (1<<20)|(1<<16)); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, local_wr);\n  rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if (rdata_grp!=0) test_err++;\n  write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIOx_INTR); GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88).","gp0_gpio_8, gpio_9, gpio_10, gpio_11, gpio_12, gpio_13, gpio_14, gpio_15, gpio_16, gpio_17, gpio_18, gpio_19, gpio_20, gpio_21, gpio_22, gpio_23, gpio_24, gpio_25, gpio_26, gpio_27, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1, INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, INTR_EN1, RAW_STCR1","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR","- Each targeted GPIO pin (8–39) shall assert an interrupt on a falling edge without timing out; ISR must execute and clear the software pending flag within the timeout window.
- Group interrupt status (INTR1_INTR_STS1) shall set the expected bit for the active pin and return to 0 after ISR raw-clear operations.
- Per-pin raw status shall be cleared by the ISR, and the system RAW_STCR1 bit for the corresponding GPIO instance shall be cleared successfully.
- Overall result: PASS if all pins meet the above without any timeout or status-clear failures; otherwise FAIL.","- Timeout failure: while(int_pend && timeout--) → if timeout==0 then test_err++.
- Group status set: (read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) & (1<<i)) != 0.
- Group status clear: read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) == 0 after raw clear.
- System raw clear: After write to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 with instance bit, subsequent read indicates bit cleared; else test_err++.
- Test conclusion: finish(test_err) where 0 indicates PASS.","Not","#include <stdio.h>
#include <lss_sysreg.h>
#include \"test_define.c\"
#include <test_common.h>
#include <gpio/gpio_def.h>
#include <gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define CNT 49","const unsigned long int addr_array[20]={MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26,MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27,};

const int default_value_array[20]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_DEFAULT_VAL,};

const int read_mask_array[20]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_READ_MASK,};

const int write_mask_array[20]={GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26_WRITE_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27_WRITE_MASK,};"},
{"path":"Test_Output/GPIO/TestPlan/GPIO_TestPlan.xlsx","content":"Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
\"3\",\"GPIO\",\"Programmable interrupt generation\",\"test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en\",\"Verify positive-edge interrupt functionality across GPIO pads 8–39. Enable routing of the GPIO interrupt, configure each per-pin control for posedge detection, set IO control groups to input mode, enable group interrupt, and for each pin generate a single rising edge and confirm the ISR triggers, group status sets and clears, and system raw status clears correctly.\",\"test_case(): Optionally enables GIC IRQ (87/88). Enables system interrupt routing using MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 and the instance bit. For i=0..31 writes 0x00020000 to per-pin registers at MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) to enable posedge detection. Waits 10 cycles. Programs IO control groups MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4 with 0x000000FF to set direction mode. Waits 10 cycles. Enables group interrupt via MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1=0xFFFFFFFF. For i=0..31: drives external register 0xA0243ffc low (0x00000000), waits 10; sets int_pend=1; drives 0xA0243ffc high (0xFFFFFFFF) to create a single rising edge; polls with timeout for int_pend to be cleared by ISR; on timeout logs error, increments test_err and breaks. Optionally drives low again and waits. Calls finish(test_err).
Default_IRQHandler(): Computes wr_val=1<<i and clears int_pend=0. Reads group status rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1). Masks group during service by write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0). If any group status bit is set, logs success; else logs error and increments test_err. Clears per-pin raw status by writing 0x00010000 to each MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(j*4), waits. Verifies group status cleared to 0. Clears system RAW_STCR1 for the respective GPIO instance and confirms the bit is cleared by reading back; on failure increments test_err. Re-enables group interrupt by writing 0xFFFFFFFF to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 and clears GIC IRQ (87/88).\",\"NA\",\"ISR\",\"NA\",\"NA\",\"Ensure only one rising edge is generated per iteration to avoid multiple triggers; mask group interrupt during service to prevent re-entry. IO control groups must be configured consistently with pad direction for correct edge detection. Timeouts indicate routing or configuration issues.\",\"1. Enable GIC for the target GPIO instance and route the instance interrupt in the system register (INTR_EN1 with the GPIO0/GPIO1 bit).\n2. Configure each per-pin control register (gp0_gpio_8 through gpio_39 range via base + index) for positive-edge detection; set IO control groups to the required mode.\n3. Enable group interrupt (INTR1_INTR_EN1) for all pins.\n4. For each pin, generate a single rising edge and wait for the ISR to run within the timeout; if timeout occurs, flag an error.\n5. In the ISR, verify group status (INTR1_INTR_STS1) indicates an interrupt occurred, clear all per-pin raw statuses, confirm group status returns to zero, clear the system raw status (RAW_STCR1), and re-enable group interrupt.\n6. Pass criteria: All pins trigger and clear correctly without timeouts; otherwise fail.\",\"- Optional: GIC_EnableIRQ(87/88).\n- write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIOx_INTR).\n- For i=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4), 0x00020000); wait_on(10).\n- write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, 0x000000FF); wait_on(10).\n- write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0xFFFFFFFF).\n- For i=0..31: write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0x00000000); wait_on(10); int_pend=1; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); poll with timeout while(int_pend==1) wait_on(10); on timeout log error and increment test_err; drive low and wait.\n- Default_IRQHandler(): wr_val=1<<i; int_pend=0; rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0);\n  If (rdata_grp & 0xFFFFFFFF)!=0 → OK else error.\n  For j=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(j*4), 0x00010000); wait_on(2);\n  rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); expect 0.\n  write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIOx_INTR); verify cleared by readback; re-enable MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1=0xFFFFFFFF; GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88).","gp0_gpio_8, gpio_9, gpio_10, gpio_11, gpio_12, gpio_13, gpio_14, gpio_15, gpio_16, gpio_17, gpio_18, gpio_19, gpio_20, gpio_21, gpio_22, gpio_23, gpio_24, gpio_25, gpio_26, gpio_27, INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, INTR_EN1, RAW_STCR1","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR","- Each GPIO pin (8–39) must generate a positive-edge interrupt that is handled by the ISR without timeout.
- Group interrupt status (INTR1_INTR_STS1) must indicate an interrupt occurred and must clear to zero after the ISR clears per-pin raw status.
- System raw interrupt status (RAW_STCR1) for the instance must be cleared successfully during ISR processing.
- Overall result: PASS if all pins meet the above; otherwise FAIL.","- Timeout failure: loop while(int_pend==1 && --timeout>0); if timeout hits 0, error.
- Group status set/clear: (read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) & 0xFFFFFFFF)!=0 on entry; equals 0 after raw clear loop.
- System raw clear: After writing to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 with instance bit, subsequent read does not retain the bit.
- Test conclusion: finish(test_err) where 0 indicates PASS.","Not","#include <lss_sysreg.h>
